WEBVTT

00:00:10.690 --> 00:00:13.860
It's an ordinary morning like any other.

00:00:14.410 --> 00:00:15.410
But...

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:18.370
Good morning!

00:00:26.790 --> 00:00:29.210
To me, it's different.

00:00:38.470 --> 00:00:40.060
I made a choice...

00:00:41.390 --> 00:00:44.940
...to create new memories here.

00:00:47.770 --> 00:00:48.690
Okay.

00:00:48.690 --> 00:00:50.070
Hasekura-kun.

00:00:51.110 --> 00:00:53.860
Oh, ah...

00:00:53.860 --> 00:00:55.570
Good morning, Vice Prez.

00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:01.640
Kizunairo kokoro to kokoro

00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:01.640
The color of bonds binding hearts to hearts

00:01:01.640 --> 00:01:04.850
Yakusoku no basho kitto michibiku wa

00:01:01.640 --> 00:01:04.850
Will surely lead us to the Promised Land.

00:01:05.190 --> 00:01:09.110
Tsutaetai tsutaekirenai

00:01:05.190 --> 00:01:09.110
I want to tell you, but I can't.

00:01:09.110 --> 00:01:13.110
Hatenai omoi ha anata...

00:01:09.110 --> 00:01:13.110
I always long for you...

00:01:18.950 --> 00:01:23.540
Boukansha no hibi ni yuuki wo dashitara sayonara

00:01:18.950 --> 00:01:23.540
Say goodbye to the days of just being a bystander.

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:32.590
Demo "jiyuu" no teigi ni buranko no you ni yureteru no ne?

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:32.590
But am I swaying over the meaning of "Freedom", like a swing?

00:01:33.260 --> 00:01:37.720
Gosenfu ni kaita kaidan

00:01:33.260 --> 00:01:37.720
Stairs drawn on a music score,

00:01:37.720 --> 00:01:41.220
Ippo susunde niho sagattemo

00:01:37.720 --> 00:01:41.220
Even if I go down one step and back two steps,

00:01:41.220 --> 00:01:45.230
Honno chotto setsunasa utau

00:01:41.220 --> 00:01:45.230
The notes play a sad melody.

00:01:45.230 --> 00:01:48.270
Watashi no real kanjite ne

00:01:45.230 --> 00:01:48.270
Hear my reality!

00:01:48.730 --> 00:01:52.190
Kizunairo kokoro to kokoro

00:01:48.730 --> 00:01:52.190
The color of bonds binding hearts to hearts

00:01:52.190 --> 00:01:55.740
Yakusoku no basho kitto michibikuwa

00:01:52.190 --> 00:01:55.740
Will surely lead us to the Promised Land.

00:01:55.740 --> 00:01:59.700
Tsutaetai tsutaekirenai

00:01:55.740 --> 00:01:59.700
I want to tell you, but can't

00:01:59.700 --> 00:02:03.120
Zutto anata wo sagashiteta

00:01:59.700 --> 00:02:03.120
I've always been searching for you.

00:02:03.740 --> 00:02:07.210
Tatoeba sou anataga hikari

00:02:03.740 --> 00:02:07.210
Let's say you are the light

00:02:07.210 --> 00:02:10.670
Watashi ga kagede mitsume aetanara

00:02:07.210 --> 00:02:10.670
And I'm the shadow, gazing at one other.

00:02:10.670 --> 00:02:14.710
Namida iro no diamond

00:02:10.670 --> 00:02:14.710
The tear-colored diamond

00:02:14.710 --> 00:02:18.510
Nee zero kara kagayakasetai

00:02:14.710 --> 00:02:18.510
I want to make it shine from nothing.

00:02:18.510 --> 00:02:24.060
Kowagaranaide musunde ne ai wo

00:02:18.510 --> 00:02:24.060
Don't be afraid of falling in love.

00:02:24.060 --> 00:02:26.230
Deaiwo...

00:02:24.230 --> 00:02:26.230
Nor of meeting people...

00:02:28.160 --> 00:02:33.000
The Newcomer

00:02:29.080 --> 00:02:35.130
So, for Hasekura-kun, who will be sharing the fun and hardships of the Student Council starting today,

00:02:35.550 --> 00:02:38.550
let me explain matters with respect to vampires.

00:02:40.010 --> 00:02:41.340
First...

00:02:46.220 --> 00:02:50.480
Please distance yourself from these stereotypical images.

00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:51.730
Okay...

00:02:54.980 --> 00:02:55.690
Shiro.

00:02:55.690 --> 00:02:56.980
Ah, yes!

00:02:57.490 --> 00:02:58.940
H-Here's your tea.

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:01.030
Thank you, Shiro-chan.

00:03:01.030 --> 00:03:05.580
So you know, Sei and Shiro-chan know we're vampires.

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:08.700
The Sendous and Togis have a long-standing history.

00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:10.960
I see.

00:03:11.460 --> 00:03:14.540
To name the characteristics of vampires:

00:03:14.540 --> 00:03:17.250
high physical capabilities,

00:03:17.250 --> 00:03:19.590
high resistance to illnesses,

00:03:19.590 --> 00:03:20.720
and immortality.

00:03:20.720 --> 00:03:22.130
Immortality?

00:03:22.130 --> 00:03:24.510
As in we don't die of old age.

00:03:24.510 --> 00:03:28.430
If I were human, I'd probably have the world record for oldest man alive.

00:03:28.430 --> 00:03:31.560
I-I'm the same age as you.

00:03:31.560 --> 00:03:36.610
W-We're not repulsed by garlic, nor will we turn to ash under the morning sun.

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:43.610
W-Well... I'm not sure what would happen if we were stabbed by a stake to the heart.

00:03:43.610 --> 00:03:46.740
Basically, we don't have any weaknesses.

00:03:46.740 --> 00:03:47.660
Hot.

00:03:48.870 --> 00:03:50.910
Though, limited to Erika, there's hot food.

00:03:50.910 --> 00:03:52.000
Well, sorry!

00:03:55.250 --> 00:03:58.550
Other than that, we're capable of erasing memories...

00:03:58.550 --> 00:04:00.630
...And we crave blood.

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:02.840
Blood?

00:04:02.840 --> 00:04:07.050
But we can get a hold of blood set aside for transfusions, so we don't have any trouble with daily life.

00:04:07.050 --> 00:04:10.220
It's not elegant at all to directly suck blood.

00:04:10.220 --> 00:04:12.440
That's a personal opinion.

00:04:12.890 --> 00:04:18.520
I only go after people on rare occasions, so don't worry.

00:04:20.320 --> 00:04:22.110
On rare occasions?

00:04:22.110 --> 00:04:26.160
Do you... have to drink blood?

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:27.620
Yes.

00:04:27.620 --> 00:04:32.000
Actually, even we don't know the details.

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:34.750
Like why we crave blood.

00:04:34.750 --> 00:04:35.960
Really...

00:04:38.630 --> 00:04:41.380
That's a crash course for you.

00:04:42.340 --> 00:04:48.180
Therefore, please be a good supporter for Erika, Hasekura-kun.

00:04:49.470 --> 00:04:53.930
After all, you two have seen each other's pure forms.

00:04:56.350 --> 00:04:57.730
Were you just remembering it?

00:04:57.730 --> 00:04:59.690
Good thing you kept your memory.

00:05:01.690 --> 00:05:03.740
Keep your mouth shut.

00:05:04.780 --> 00:05:07.280
You, too. Don't recall it.

00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:09.330
It's easier said than done.

00:05:09.330 --> 00:05:11.540
I know this is sudden, but Hasekura-kun...

00:05:12.410 --> 00:05:16.120
...as a new member to the Student Council, there's something I want you to do.

00:05:21.130 --> 00:05:27.380
So, this is Hasekura Kouhei-kun,
the lead organizer of the Sports Festival.

00:05:22.300 --> 00:05:27.800
Sports Festival Executive
Committee Meeting

00:05:29.180 --> 00:05:32.310
You're not going to do it like last year, Prez?

00:05:32.310 --> 00:05:34.560
I was looking forward to it...

00:05:35.180 --> 00:05:36.810
I'm the lead organizer?

00:05:36.810 --> 00:05:37.940
What are you thinking?

00:05:37.940 --> 00:05:44.940
To have you learn how the Student Council works,
it's best to put you in a role with some responsibilities.

00:05:44.940 --> 00:05:46.200
Even so...

00:05:47.200 --> 00:05:49.160
Customs make it easy.

00:05:49.160 --> 00:05:50.740
Wait-

00:05:58.710 --> 00:06:01.000
I said I was going to change.

00:06:01.750 --> 00:06:05.090
I'm Hasekura Kouhei, the lead organizer.

00:06:05.090 --> 00:06:08.430
I've only just transferred to this school in April.

00:06:08.430 --> 00:06:12.390
To be honest, I know nothing about this school's Sports Festival.

00:06:14.890 --> 00:06:19.770
But I'm told by the President that many of you were part of this committee last year.

00:06:19.770 --> 00:06:25.530
Therefore I'd like to hear as much of your input as possible.

00:06:25.530 --> 00:06:26.990
Look at that.

00:06:28.030 --> 00:06:35.290
On my end, due to the multiple school transfers I've been through, I've seen many Sports Festivals.

00:06:35.740 --> 00:06:41.880
I'd like to implement events that were fun and
create moving moments that I've experienced.

00:06:41.880 --> 00:06:44.300
I hope we can organize a good event.

00:06:55.470 --> 00:06:58.100
Making a merit from a demerit.

00:06:58.100 --> 00:07:01.020
It's good way to attract the audience's attention.

00:07:03.520 --> 00:07:04.650
So, how did it go?

00:07:04.650 --> 00:07:09.030
They managed to assign roles to people.

00:07:09.650 --> 00:07:13.490
For a first meeting, he did well.

00:07:13.490 --> 00:07:15.780
For that...

00:07:17.080 --> 00:07:20.120
Hasekura. You didn't fill out the requisition form correctly.

00:07:20.120 --> 00:07:21.170
Redo it.

00:07:21.960 --> 00:07:23.250
I'm sorry.

00:07:23.790 --> 00:07:27.920
Of course, coming up with original programs, selecting the BGM, and so on...

00:07:27.920 --> 00:07:30.970
There's a mountain of things to do.

00:07:31.550 --> 00:07:33.890
But you can't disturb him.

00:07:33.890 --> 00:07:35.350
Nii-san!

00:07:35.930 --> 00:07:38.890
Pampering people isn't always best for them.

00:07:38.890 --> 00:07:42.350
And that's more the case for fellow Student Council members.

00:07:42.350 --> 00:07:43.650
Am I wrong?

00:07:49.490 --> 00:07:51.570
Please enjoy, Hasekura-senpai.

00:07:51.570 --> 00:07:52.610
Thank you.

00:07:56.870 --> 00:07:58.910
He looks really busy.

00:07:58.910 --> 00:07:59.870
Yes...

00:08:01.580 --> 00:08:05.130
B-But he's now part of the Student Council.

00:08:05.130 --> 00:08:06.880
We need him to work hard.

00:08:20.770 --> 00:08:22.230
It's already this late?

00:08:28.440 --> 00:08:29.730
Yahoo!

00:08:29.730 --> 00:08:33.490
It's another mesmerizing night for a tea party.

00:08:36.990 --> 00:08:37.910
Kouhei?

00:08:38.410 --> 00:08:39.830
Kouhei-kun?

00:08:41.330 --> 00:08:43.290
You joined the Student Council?!

00:08:43.290 --> 00:08:44.290
Yes.

00:08:44.790 --> 00:08:48.920
I wasn't trying to hide it or anything;
I just couldn't find the time to tell you.

00:08:48.920 --> 00:08:53.720
On top of that, you were forced into becoming the lead organizer for the Sports Festival.

00:08:53.720 --> 00:08:55.050
My condolences.

00:08:56.390 --> 00:09:00.470
Now that's definitely like Iorin, drafting Kouhei already.

00:09:00.470 --> 00:09:04.480
I had my eyes on you first, you know.

00:09:04.480 --> 00:09:08.940
It's amazing how you're already working as a lead organizer.

00:09:08.940 --> 00:09:12.570
But, I never thought it was this much work.

00:09:13.150 --> 00:09:14.900
Am I okay for this position?

00:09:14.900 --> 00:09:17.160
Let's change the order of the words.

00:09:18.280 --> 00:09:19.870
It's not "Am I".

00:09:19.870 --> 00:09:21.370
It's "I am".

00:09:21.370 --> 00:09:24.540
I'm sure there are things that can be done because it's you.

00:09:24.540 --> 00:09:25.790
Because it's me...

00:09:25.790 --> 00:09:29.210
Yup. I'll give you my words.

00:09:29.750 --> 00:09:32.630
Anyway, you'll do just fine.

00:09:32.630 --> 00:09:34.340
Remember that time, too?

00:09:34.340 --> 00:09:35.880
That time?

00:09:35.880 --> 00:09:40.430
When you tried to see how far you could go with your hands off the bicycle handle.

00:09:40.430 --> 00:09:43.680
You kept going until you kissed the ground.

00:09:43.680 --> 00:09:47.730
That's not working hard; that's just being reckless.

00:09:47.730 --> 00:09:50.980
Reckless it may be, but what's important is the challenging mind.

00:09:51.480 --> 00:09:54.650
A new record may be born from that.

00:09:56.110 --> 00:09:57.490
I guess.

00:09:57.490 --> 00:10:00.120
But leave kissing the ground out.

00:10:11.170 --> 00:10:13.420
Good luck, Kouhei-kun.

00:10:14.210 --> 00:10:19.550
I'm sure it'll be tough working as the lead organizer, but let me know if there's anything I can help with.

00:10:20.140 --> 00:10:25.560
Thanks. I keep finding myself being cheered on by you.

00:10:25.560 --> 00:10:27.310
That's not true.

00:10:27.890 --> 00:10:34.480
Remember, when I couldn't do a back hip circle, you cheered me on.

00:10:36.940 --> 00:10:38.150
Oh yeah.

00:10:38.150 --> 00:10:40.860
There was that.

00:10:49.670 --> 00:10:51.420
Hasekura

00:10:49.670 --> 00:10:51.580
Yuuki
Haruna

00:10:49.670 --> 00:10:58.090
Dear Haruna, thanks for the letter. Right after I got to my new school they gave us an Arithmetic test and I completely bombed it. The sports classes are fun though. In your last letter you told me that you weren't able to do the back hip circle. Don't give up on them! With enough practice I'm sure you'll be doing them in no time!

00:10:58.090 --> 00:10:58.380
Dear Haruna, thanks for the letter. Right after I got to my new school they gave us an Arithmetic test and I completely bombed it. The sports classes are fun though. In your last letter you told me that you weren't able to do the back hip circle. Don't give up on them! With enough practice I'm sure you'll be doing them in no time!

00:11:05.140 --> 00:11:06.100
Bye!

00:11:06.100 --> 00:11:07.810
See you later, Erika!

00:11:07.810 --> 00:11:09.180
Yup, bye!

00:11:12.940 --> 00:11:14.650
Wh-What's this?!

00:11:15.360 --> 00:11:18.610
I need to familiarize myself with past Sports Festivals.

00:11:18.610 --> 00:11:21.280
Otherwise I won't know what I can do.

00:11:21.280 --> 00:11:24.120
Youth is great.

00:11:24.120 --> 00:11:28.500
Oh, and if you could sort the old reference materials while you're at it, that'd be great.

00:11:28.500 --> 00:11:29.870
I'm on it.

00:11:29.870 --> 00:11:30.960
How reliable.

00:11:34.710 --> 00:11:35.960
Gosh.

00:11:37.710 --> 00:11:39.010
I'll go, too.

00:11:39.010 --> 00:11:41.470
Shiro. Get us some tea.

00:11:42.840 --> 00:11:43.970
Nii-sama...

00:11:45.180 --> 00:11:46.350
Yes.

00:11:53.440 --> 00:11:54.270
Hey.

00:11:54.270 --> 00:11:56.360
It's faster with an extra set of hands, right?

00:11:56.360 --> 00:11:58.320
Vice Prez.

00:11:58.320 --> 00:11:59.570
Thank you.

00:12:02.240 --> 00:12:08.700
If I'm right, there are unorganized
Sports Festival related materials up here.

00:12:18.130 --> 00:12:19.250
Are you all right?

00:12:19.250 --> 00:12:20.210
Yes...

00:12:25.840 --> 00:12:26.850
I'm sorry!

00:12:26.850 --> 00:12:29.220
No. It's fine. It's fine.

00:12:37.610 --> 00:12:38.690
Look.

00:12:39.690 --> 00:12:41.990
It's true he's immortal.

00:12:42.570 --> 00:12:45.490
He hasn't changed at all, like how he stands out, too.

00:12:45.490 --> 00:12:46.620
Hey look.

00:12:52.160 --> 00:12:54.210
Everyone looks like they're having lots of fun.

00:12:55.790 --> 00:12:56.750
Yeah.

00:12:57.750 --> 00:13:01.960
I wonder if I can make everyone smile like this, too.

00:13:03.050 --> 00:13:10.140
It's up to us, the stage crew, to make a school where everyone can have a better time.

00:13:10.140 --> 00:13:14.350
So... I hope everyone's smiling like them.

00:13:35.660 --> 00:13:36.670
Okay!

00:14:03.530 --> 00:14:05.940
Hasekura-senpai's working very hard.

00:14:06.780 --> 00:14:09.360
He's rather popular in my class, too.

00:14:09.360 --> 00:14:13.290
Everyone says he's a lead organizer who is proactive.

00:14:13.290 --> 00:14:14.750
Really?

00:14:15.660 --> 00:14:19.210
So everyone can have a better school life.

00:14:20.250 --> 00:14:23.000
It's Hasekura-kun's motto of late.

00:14:23.000 --> 00:14:24.800
Great words, don't you think?

00:14:24.800 --> 00:14:27.380
I wonder who he picked it up from.

00:14:33.100 --> 00:14:34.390
Hasekura-kun...

00:14:37.600 --> 00:14:41.940
It's a proper mindset for the lead organizer. Yeah.

00:14:47.780 --> 00:14:50.740
You're still hung up over the Sports Festival program?

00:14:50.740 --> 00:14:53.490
You don't have many days left.

00:14:53.490 --> 00:14:58.000
It's pretty much ready, but I'm wondering if there are any more interesting events.

00:14:58.000 --> 00:15:01.000
I want to make it as fun as possible.

00:15:01.000 --> 00:15:02.880
I see...

00:15:04.420 --> 00:15:05.670
How about this?

00:15:05.670 --> 00:15:08.970
Electro-bomb! Barbed Wire Death Match Cavalry!

00:15:08.970 --> 00:15:12.010
I'm sure everyone will be desperate!

00:15:12.010 --> 00:15:13.720
Do you have any good ideas?

00:15:14.720 --> 00:15:17.060
He ignored me!

00:15:22.730 --> 00:15:24.730
Here you go, Kouhei-kun.

00:15:25.480 --> 00:15:26.980
It's honey juice.

00:15:26.980 --> 00:15:31.360
It looks like you're stressed out, so take a sip when you're tired.

00:15:31.360 --> 00:15:32.410
It's good!

00:15:32.410 --> 00:15:33.820
Thank you, Haruna.

00:15:33.820 --> 00:15:36.620
Nice assist, Hina-chan!

00:15:36.620 --> 00:15:38.120
You go, my bride!

00:15:38.120 --> 00:15:39.700
Oh, come on, Onee-chan.

00:15:39.700 --> 00:15:42.830
It's a reward from Hina-chan for working so hard.

00:15:42.830 --> 00:15:43.920
Aren't you lucky.

00:15:46.420 --> 00:15:47.750
A reward, huh?

00:15:52.300 --> 00:15:55.600
How about asking the shopping district to become sponsors?

00:15:55.600 --> 00:15:56.850
The shopping district?

00:15:56.850 --> 00:15:58.060
Sponsors?

00:15:58.060 --> 00:15:59.100
What do you have in mind?

00:16:00.390 --> 00:16:07.900
At one of my old schools, they gave out prizes for events and found sponsors from the local shopping district.

00:16:07.900 --> 00:16:12.070
Even if it wasn't something grand, little prizes made everyone happy.

00:16:12.780 --> 00:16:18.950
So how about we ask the shopping district on Tamatsu Island to sponsor some prizes?

00:16:19.450 --> 00:16:23.460
And if we invite the people on this island, I think it would make things very interesting.

00:16:23.460 --> 00:16:25.420
Prizes, huh...

00:16:25.420 --> 00:16:27.920
Sure, it may make things interesting...

00:16:27.920 --> 00:16:31.670
Yeah, but... We've never done that at this school before...

00:16:31.670 --> 00:16:33.680
Trying to implement that at this stage?

00:16:41.850 --> 00:16:45.230
If it's never been done before,
I just have to make this the first time.

00:16:47.150 --> 00:16:48.730
Hasekura-senpai!

00:16:50.530 --> 00:16:51.780
Shiro-chan.

00:16:51.780 --> 00:16:53.030
Why are you here?

00:16:53.030 --> 00:16:57.780
Um... Please let me help you!

00:17:02.000 --> 00:17:03.750
Shuuchikan Academy Sports Festival
Special Project

00:17:02.000 --> 00:17:03.750
Responsibility: Shuuchikan Academy Student Council
and Sports Festival Executive Committee

00:17:02.000 --> 00:17:03.750
※Project Summary

00:17:02.000 --> 00:17:03.750
Our aim is to transcend the framework of an event run by an

00:17:02.000 --> 00:17:03.750
individual school and, through the participation and cooperation

00:17:02.000 --> 00:17:03.750
of everyone in the Tamatsu Seafront Shopping District, elevate

00:17:02.000 --> 00:17:03.750
the festival to a position of region-wide significance.

00:17:02.000 --> 00:17:03.750
※Project Details

00:17:02.000 --> 00:17:03.750
We will receive goods from each shop in the Tamatsu Seafront

00:17:02.000 --> 00:17:03.750
Shopping District to offer as prizes to competitors. In return,

00:17:02.000 --> 00:17:03.750
the names of contributing shops will be announced at the venue.

00:17:15.430 --> 00:17:15.550
Math

00:17:15.930 --> 00:17:16.050
English

00:17:21.970 --> 00:17:26.350
This area looks really different from the shopping district.

00:17:26.350 --> 00:17:30.480
Yes. Houses around here have been around for many years.

00:17:40.410 --> 00:17:42.790
Oh, I see.

00:17:42.790 --> 00:17:48.250
If it's a request from Shiro-sama, we'd be happy to help out.

00:17:48.250 --> 00:17:50.040
Shiro-sama?

00:17:57.130 --> 00:17:58.970
We managed to gather a lot more than expected.

00:17:59.470 --> 00:18:01.300
It's thanks to your recommendations, too.

00:18:01.300 --> 00:18:04.720
Oh no. It's all your hard work.

00:18:04.720 --> 00:18:07.100
Really, you were a great help.

00:18:07.850 --> 00:18:08.850
But honestly...

00:18:10.310 --> 00:18:12.650
"Shiro-sama" was a surprise.

00:18:12.650 --> 00:18:14.610
Th-That's...

00:18:15.570 --> 00:18:20.240
I'm told that the Togi family has always been a prominent family on this island.

00:18:20.240 --> 00:18:22.160
So that's why you're Shiro-sama.

00:18:23.080 --> 00:18:29.750
I've been strictly raised by Nii-sama as befitting a Togi.

00:18:37.630 --> 00:18:44.470
That's not really the reason,
but I've hardly ever left this island.

00:18:44.470 --> 00:18:50.770
It's the opposite of you; I don't know much about anything off this island.

00:18:51.520 --> 00:18:54.820
Then we should take a trip with everyone.

00:18:56.400 --> 00:18:59.570
I need to thank you for helping me out today, too.

00:19:00.240 --> 00:19:02.530
I'll give you a tour off the island one of these days.

00:19:03.120 --> 00:19:04.530
Really?!

00:19:04.530 --> 00:19:07.290
Thank you very much, Hasekura-senpai!

00:19:08.500 --> 00:19:11.330
The same goes for me. Thanks for your work today.

00:19:11.330 --> 00:19:12.130
Yes!

00:19:24.140 --> 00:19:25.930
Sports Festival Opening!
finally here tomorrow!!

00:19:30.560 --> 00:19:30.940
Shuuchikan Academy
Sports Festival

00:19:30.560 --> 00:19:32.940
Equipment Budget Report

00:19:30.560 --> 00:19:32.940
Safety Measure Report

00:19:30.560 --> 00:19:32.940
Processed

00:19:38.360 --> 00:19:40.570
I wonder if he's still at it.

00:19:58.050 --> 00:19:59.300
He's like a child.

00:19:59.840 --> 00:20:02.130
I guess I'll give him a hand.

00:20:02.130 --> 00:20:04.260
You're taking too much long, Boss.

00:20:04.260 --> 00:20:06.640
We're all done with our work.

00:20:06.640 --> 00:20:08.260
Let's finish this thing up.

00:20:08.260 --> 00:20:10.560
Boss, you want it like this, right?

00:20:10.560 --> 00:20:14.520
Boss, can you run one last check through the prizes?

00:20:14.520 --> 00:20:15.650
Let me see.

00:20:17.570 --> 00:20:18.980
Does it look okay?

00:20:19.900 --> 00:20:22.150
I think you're off by a digit here.

00:20:24.990 --> 00:20:28.240
Everyone's gathered around Hasekura-senpai.

00:20:28.240 --> 00:20:30.660
He's such an amazing person.

00:20:33.620 --> 00:20:36.790
Like I said, he's the lead organizer, so it's to be expected.

00:20:39.460 --> 00:20:41.510
Okay, let's carry this away.

00:20:41.510 --> 00:20:42.630
Yeah!

00:20:43.340 --> 00:20:44.680
We should go, too.

00:20:44.680 --> 00:20:45.760
Yes.

00:20:46.640 --> 00:20:50.890
One, two. One, two. One, two.

00:20:51.890 --> 00:20:53.890
So the gate's ready?!

00:20:53.890 --> 00:20:57.940
Charge! You come, too, Heiji!

00:20:57.940 --> 00:20:59.400
Me, too?

00:20:59.400 --> 00:21:03.650
One, two. One, two.

00:21:03.650 --> 00:21:05.160
One, two.

00:21:16.420 --> 00:21:19.420
Sports

00:21:16.420 --> 00:21:19.420
Festival

00:21:24.050 --> 00:21:26.090
Everyone's got good looks on their faces.

00:21:30.600 --> 00:21:33.100
I haven't seen Erika that happy in a while.

00:21:33.600 --> 00:21:37.020
So everything is going as you planned?

00:21:38.560 --> 00:21:41.860
Looks like he was the right choice.

00:22:07.180 --> 00:22:14.520
I miss you

00:22:24.940 --> 00:22:34.580
Mabushii kurai e ni kaita jikan nano

00:22:24.940 --> 00:22:34.580
Just like in a perfect painting,

00:22:34.580 --> 00:22:39.330
Sou ima ha...

00:22:34.580 --> 00:22:39.330
Now is a dazzling moment.

00:22:43.630 --> 00:22:53.390
Kawari hajimeta machinami ni me wo sorashi

00:22:43.630 --> 00:22:53.390
I look away from the city that's starting to change

00:22:53.390 --> 00:22:59.100
Omoide ha tada iuno

00:22:53.390 --> 00:22:59.100
And my memories whisper to me, saying,

00:22:59.100 --> 00:23:06.230
Soko de tomadou dake

00:22:59.100 --> 00:23:06.230
You're only at a loss.

00:23:06.230 --> 00:23:08.240
I miss you

00:23:08.240 --> 00:23:12.490
Omoi wo sono mama dakishimete

00:23:08.240 --> 00:23:12.490
Hold on to your feelings.

00:23:12.490 --> 00:23:14.410
I miss you

00:23:14.410 --> 00:23:18.750
Kawaranu omoi wo shiritai no

00:23:14.410 --> 00:23:18.750
I want to know how you've always felt.

00:23:18.750 --> 00:23:20.620
I miss you

00:23:20.620 --> 00:23:24.380
Negatteru kara

00:23:20.620 --> 00:23:24.380
I'll always long for you, so...

00:23:24.920 --> 00:23:30.380
I miss you...

00:23:38.140 --> 00:23:39.350
Tomorrow's the day!

00:23:39.480 --> 00:23:41.350
Let's keep this up, everyone!

00:23:41.600 --> 00:23:43.520
Yeah!

00:23:57.660 --> 00:24:00.830
One last bit to go!

00:24:00.830 --> 00:24:03.170
Yeah...

00:24:05.040 --> 00:24:20.060
「Key」

00:24:05.290 --> 00:24:20.060
Fifth Episode

00:24:06.290 --> 00:24:09.010
Let's speak from the belly.

00:24:09.010 --> 00:24:12.510
The sun is a dryer for a damp heart.

00:24:12.550 --> 00:24:15.470
Squeeze the melancholy out,

00:24:15.510 --> 00:24:16.180
and look!

00:24:16.180 --> 00:24:18.890
A shower of smiles feels so good!
